7:["$","ol",null,{"style":{"paddingLeft":"1.25rem","lineHeight":"1.9"},"children":[["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Kaikondrahalli Lake"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Sarjapur Road, East Bangalore"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"Most Bangaloreans will cite Ulsoor or Hebbal as the city's lakes — but Kaikondrahalli is the one that was actually restored by residents themselves. The community effort shows: there's a proper walking path, nesting birds, a small amphitheatre, and almost no litter. Early mornings here feel genuinely peaceful in a way that's rare in this city."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Kempe Gowda Watchtower, Lalbagh"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Lalbagh, South Bangalore"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"Most people who visit Lalbagh walk right past this. Built in the 16th century by the founder of Bangalore, the watchtower sits on a rocky hillock inside the garden. Climb to the top and you get one of the most unexpected city views in Bangalore — old trees below, glass towers in the distance. Entry is included in the Lalbagh entry fee."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Bhoomi College Library (open hours)"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Kanakapura Road, South Bangalore"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"Bhoomi is an ecological learning centre that occasionally opens its extensive library to the public. The collection focuses on ecology, sustainability, and Indian natural history — many volumes you won't find on any e-commerce platform. Call ahead to confirm access. The campus itself, surrounded by forest, is worth the 45-minute drive from the city."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Hesaraghatta Grasslands"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— ~30 km north of Bangalore, Hesaraghatta"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"One of the last remaining grassland ecosystems near Bangalore and a critical habitat for birds like the Indian Bustard and Pallid Harrier. Serious birders have been coming here for decades. There's no formal entry structure — which is part of why it remains unspoiled. Go with a birding group if you can; the Bangalore Bird Club does regular walks here."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Government Museum Annexe"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Kasturba Road, CBD"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"The main Visvesvaraya Industrial Museum gets all the attention, but the Government Museum next door — one of the oldest in India, dating to 1865 — is almost always empty. Rooms full of Indus Valley artefacts, Hoysala sculptures, and bronze-age tools, with almost no crowds. Entry is around ₹20. Budget an unhurried two hours."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Jayamahal Palace Hotel Garden"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#888"},"children":"— Jayamahal, North Bangalore"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"marginTop":"0.25rem"},"children":"A heritage property that's now a hotel — but the garden is accessible if you walk in and order a coffee at the cafe. The architecture is old Indo-Saracenic, the grounds are quiet on weekday afternoons, and it feels completely removed from the surrounding neighbourhood. One of Bangalore's best-kept secrets for a slow afternoon."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"1.5rem"},"children":["$Le"," ","$Lf","$L10"]}]]}]
8:["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1.4rem","fontWeight":600,"margin":"2rem 0 1rem"},"children":"The City Rewards Curiosity"}]
9:["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":"1.8","marginBottom":"1rem"},"children":"Most of these places don't advertise. There are no influencer reels with 2 million views pointing you toward the Kempe Gowda watchtower or the Hesaraghatta grasslands. That's exactly why they're still worth going to. Bangalore's hidden places have survived precisely because they haven't been discovered at scale."}]
a:["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":"1.8"},"children":"If you know of a place that belongs on this list and isn't here — we want to hear about it."}]
b:["$","$L11",null,{"children":["$L12",["$","$L13",null,{"promise":"$@14"}]]}]
